&#8220;I remember one time Chris Lighty called me up. He was like, &#8216;Yo, you gotta come down here. You gotta come to Chung King Studios,'&#8221; he said. &#8220;&#8216;For some reason, Ol&#8217; Dirty Bastard just came in here, broke all your plaques and pissed on &#8217;em.'&#8221;

While others would&#8217;ve been angry at the situation, LL could only laugh, as some things aren&#8217;t meant to be understood when it comes to ODB. The plaque smashing somehow even added to their friendship.

&#8220;I said, ‘What I do?’ I didn&#8217;t even understand it,&#8221; he continued. &#8220;I couldn&#8217;t understand it. Loved him ever since. Shout out to Ol&#8217; Dirty, man!&#8221;

Before his death, Chris Lighty provided more context on ODB&#8217;s outburst at Chung King Studios in an interview with Stuff Magazine in 2006.

&#8220;[Ol&#8217; Dirty Bastard] came through twisted. He was talking gibberish on his rhyme and then gets mad at us because we weren&#8217;t gonna record him like that,&#8221; he said. &#8220;He started ripping gold and platinum plaques off the wall. And he definitely pissed on one of the plaques.&#8221;

The late music executive added: &#8220;At this point, he&#8217;s off the Richter scale. The receptionist calls the police, so we get out of there. At the bottom of the elevator, he changes his whole tune. He was laughing his a&#8211; off!&#8221;

ODB died at 35 years old in November 2004 due to an accidental drug overdose after collapsing at RZA&#8217;s recording studio in NYC.

As for LL Cool J, he&#8217;s gearing up to host his Rock the Bells Festival , which is slated to hit Long Island&#8217;s UBS Arena on Aug. 15. A lineup for the festival is yet to be announced.

